WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.583
The next morning in school I told Mrs. Romano about my new invention.

2
00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:22.145
Then I showed her Molly's pink flower.

3
00:00:22.146 --> 00:00:27.857
"Why, Iggy," she said. "What a marvelous idea!"

4
00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:32.046
"Can I put the flower on your glasses?" I asked.

5
00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:39.032
Mrs. Romano nodded so I wrapped the wire stem around the frames of her glasses.

6
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:43.714
When she put the glasses on, everyone started laughing.

7
00:00:43.715 --> 00:00:50.298
"Mrs. Romano, you look funny with a flower sticking up from your glasses!" cried Evan.

8
00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:56.017
"Well, at least I won't lose them," said Mrs. Romano, smiling.

9
00:00:56.018 --> 00:01:00.936
But when Mrs. Romano went to feed the goldfish, the flower fell off her glasses.

10
00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:05.747
It tumbled right into the fish tank!

11
00:01:05.748 --> 00:01:09.812
Lauren scooped it out.

12
00:01:09.813 --> 00:01:12.490
"Iggy!" cried Molly.

13
00:01:12.491 --> 00:01:15.409
"You promised to take care of my flower.

14
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.078
You didn't tell me it was going to get wet!"

15
00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.843
"I'm sorry," I said.

16
00:01:21.844 --> 00:01:25.887
"I didn't think it would fall into the fish tank."

17
00:01:25.888 --> 00:01:31.908
We put the flower on a sunny windowsill during art class so it would dry.

18
00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:39.157
When we came back from art, Mrs. Romano suggested that someone else try the Fabulous Glasses-Finder.

19
00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:43.331
"Let me try it!" said Kristin.

20
00:01:43.332 --> 00:01:47.882
That's when things really started to go wrong.

21
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:52.028
First the flower fell over Kristin's eyes and she couldn't see.

22
00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:55.735
She bumped into a desk and nearly fell over.

23
00:01:55.736 --> 00:01:59.466
Then the wire stem kept sticking her in the head.

24
00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.992
"Ouch," said Kristin, rubbing her head.

25
00:02:02.993 --> 00:02:05.442
"This thing hurts."

26
00:02:05.443 --> 00:02:09.885
Soon Kristin got tired of wearing the flower on her glasses.

27
00:02:09.886 --> 00:02:14.401
Lauren said she would wear it next.

28
00:02:14.402 --> 00:02:20.506
I attached the flower to Lauren's glasses at recess.

29
00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:25.077
She was in line for the slide when she leaned over to tie her shoe.

30
00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:29.853
That's when the flower stem got caught on Ruby's sweater.

31
00:02:29.854 --> 00:02:32.897
"Help! We're stuck together!"

32
00:02:32.898 --> 00:02:35.883
cried Ruby, trying to step away.

33
00:02:35.884 --> 00:02:43.136
"Stand still!" cried Lauren. "You're pulling my glasses off."

34
00:02:43.137 --> 00:02:47.239
"And you're ripping my sweater!" said Ruby.

35
00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.660
I finally got Ruby and Lauren unstuck.

36
00:02:50.661 --> 00:02:55.291
After that, Lauren didn't want to wear the flower on her glasses anymore.

37
00:02:55.292 --> 00:02:59.712
"That flower is nothing but trouble," she said.

38
00:02:59.713 --> 00:03:03.275
I hated to admit it, but Lauren was right.

39
00:03:03.276 --> 00:03:07.415
The Fabulous Glasses-Finder was not my greatest invention.

40
00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:11.015
In fact, it was one of my worst!

41
00:03:11.016 --> 00:03:17.558
The next day in school, we wrote down our invention ideas for Mr. Bright.

42
00:03:17.559 --> 00:03:21.272
He was going to announce the winner at the school assembly.

43
00:03:21.273 --> 00:03:26.487
Mrs. Romano said we could write down two invention ideas if we wanted to.

44
00:03:26.488 --> 00:03:30.941
But I didn't even have one invention I was excited about.

45
00:03:30.942 --> 00:03:33.585
I raised my hand.

46
00:03:33.586 --> 00:03:37.366
"Yes, Iggy?" said Mrs. Romano.

47
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:42.419
"I don't have a good invention to write about," I said.

48
00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:48.082
"What about your Fabulous Glasses-Finder?" said Mrs. Romano.

49
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:51.280
"It's a very original invention, Iggy."

50
00:03:51.281 --> 00:03:54.836
"Except that no one liked it," I mumbled.

51
00:03:54.837 --> 00:03:57.048
"It doesn't work that great."

52
00:03:57.049 --> 00:04:01.387
By now I was feeling a little sorry for myself.

53
00:04:01.388 --> 00:04:04.735
"I liked it," said Mrs. Romano.

54
00:04:04.736 --> 00:04:08.059
"Even though it did fall into the fish tank."

55
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.027
I knew Mrs. Romano was only trying to make me feel better.

56
00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:17.044
But I wrote about the Fabulous Glasses-Finder anyway.

57
00:04:17.045 --> 00:04:21.454
Ruby wrote about a rubber glove filled with sand.

58
00:04:21.455 --> 00:04:26.068
You could bend the fingers to hold rings or notes.

59
00:04:26.069 --> 00:04:29.983
Evan had an idea for an automatic fish-feeder.

60
00:04:29.984 --> 00:04:35.604
"You can feed your fish, even if you're away on vacation," he explained.

61
00:04:35.605 --> 00:04:39.583
"That's a really neat idea," said Colby.

62
00:04:39.584 --> 00:04:44.114
"Very inventive!" agreed Mrs. Romano.

63
00:04:44.115 --> 00:04:49.724
Molly wrote about a way to cut socks and use them as hand-warmers.

64
00:04:49.725 --> 00:05:02.422
And I, Iggy, wrote about a stupid glasses-finder that no one wanted to use!
